* The toy gun held by its grip (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own
* script; owner's screencast, 2026-11-27: the gun jumped about in the hand
* and was held well away from its handle). Run by openc2e after the world
* loads (Additions folder).
* any world: it changes objects by kind, not Eden's map, so it runs on every
* world (other Additions run only on worlds started from Eden.sfc).
*
* The toy gun (2 13 14, pgun: 26 pictures of 92 x 52; 0-12 facing left,
* 5-12 firing; 13-25 facing right, 18-25 firing) came with its pickup points
* one picture out: none for picture 0, and picture 13, the first facing
* right, held at the left-facing gun's handle. As its idle animation cycles,
* the point it is held by jumped from one end of the gun to the other. Every
* picture is now held by the middle of the grip, which is drawn in the same
* place in all of them, firing or not: x 75-87, y 41-50 facing left, and
* the mirror image, x 4-16, facing right.
enum 2 13 14
  setv var0 0
  reps 13
    setv puhl var0 81 45
    addv var0 1
  repe
  reps 13
    setv puhl var0 10 45
    addv var0 1
  repe
next
